  "result": "The fix is in and the tests pass. `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now clamps to a value inside the range.\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Before, `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`, and `IntRange(max=10, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `20` into `11`. Both now give `1` and `9`.\n- **Tests:** I added those two cases to the `test_range` parametrization in `tests/test_types.py`.\n- **Results:** `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py` gives 71 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Say if you want a commit, and with which attribution line.",
